// The sandbox service contract.
//
// This file is the single source for both implementations. The transitional
// Python control plane and the Go service that replaces it generate from it, so
// the two cannot drift while they coexist, and the SDK speaks one wire format
// throughout.
//
// Two rules shape it.
//
//   - Command and file traffic are absent on purpose. A create returns the
//     resolved agent endpoint and the SDK talks to the sandbox directly, because
//     an episode issues dozens of commands and a control plane in that path adds
//     a hop and a serialization without making a decision.
//   - A failure is typed by attribution rather than by where it happened. An
//     infrastructure fault that arrives as a task result would be recorded as a
//     model or harness failure and would corrupt a reward.

